{"body":"The frozen `CultureMech:004352` / KOMODO 2075 record normalizes the raw token\n`Se-acid` to `Selenic acid`. The original DSMZ 1003 trace-mineral recipe also\nprints only `Se-acid`, at 10 mg/L. Neither that label nor the concentration\nestablishes selenium(VI) selenic acid rather than selenium(IV) selenous acid.\n\nPrimary source: [DSMZ medium 1003](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1003.pdf), page 2, trace-mineral table.\n\nThe worker-02 frozen case is\n`CM_NAME:372da9d701593df754695e2c0c4ecee1c1ccd06fb368c80d59a2e699eaf43e03`.\nThe complete frozen recipe and case digest are retained in the campaign queue;\nthe captured original PDF and per-case assessment are preserved with the\nworker's evidence. The decision is unresolved because the normalization adds\nan oxidation-state claim the cited source does not establish.\n\nFollow-up:\n\n- Retain the exact `Se-acid` source label and its source identifier/occurrence.\n- Obtain an original reagent formula, CAS number, supplier label or provider\n  correction distinguishing H2SeO4 from H2SeO3.\n- Correct the normalization only from that source-specific evidence. Do not\n  replace it with selenous acid merely because that reagent is common.\n- Preserve the source hold until the exact obligation is resolved; ontology\n  term existence and matching scores do not settle this source identity.\n\nThe review does not edit CultureMech, MIM maintained data or downstream outputs.\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-08T05:25:15Z","number":675,"state":"OPEN","title":"Preserve Se-acid uncertainty in KOMODO 2075 / DSMZ 1003 normalization","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/issues/675"}
